Copyright (c) 2026 Leon Lin, MIT License. Its licence is in
crates/earshot/LICENSE-earshot. The vocabulary statistics in crates/earshot/data
are derived from earshot.

crates/earshot/src/notes.rs ports the windowing and the note creation of Basic
Pitch (https://github.com/spotify/basic-pitch), Copyright 2022 Spotify AB, Apache
License 2.0. This product includes software developed at Spotify AB
(http://www.spotify.com/). The licence and Basic Pitch's notice are in
crates/earshot/LICENSE-basic-pitch.

The studio draws its text in Inter (https://github.com/rsms/inter), Copyright (c)
2016 The Inter Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1, and its icons from
Lucide (https://lucide.dev), Copyright (c) 2026 Lucide Icons and Contributors,
ISC License, with icons from Feather, Copyright (c) 2013-present Cole Bemis, MIT
License. Both are cut down to what the studio shows, in crates/claudius-ui/assets/fonts,
with their licences beside them (LICENSE-Inter.txt, LICENSE-lucide.txt).

Rust crates the binaries link are listed with their licences in Cargo.lock and
checked by cargo-deny (deny.toml). Every one of them is under a permissive or
weak-copyleft licence (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode, MPL-2.0 for
symphonia). ONNX Runtime (MIT, Microsoft) is linked statically.


Downloaded on first use, not distributed with claudius
------------------------------------------------------

The listening models, fetched from the Hugging Face Hub (Basic Pitch's from
GitHub) by `claudius setup` or the first verdict, checked against pinned
SHA-256 hashes:

  - CLAP "larger_clap_general" by LAION, Apache-2.0
    (https://huggingface.co/laion/larger_clap_general), in the ONNX export by
    Xenova (https://huggingface.co/Xenova/larger_clap_general).
  - The Audio Spectrogram Transformer fine-tuned on AudioSet by MIT CSAIL,
    BSD-3-Clause (https://huggingface.co/MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593),
    in the ONNX export by Xenova. Only used with `--tags`.
  - Spleeter's four stems by Deezer, MIT (https://github.com/deezer/spleeter), in
    the ONNX export by Best-Practice, Apache-2.0
    (https://huggingface.co/Best-Practice/spleeter-4stems-onnx).
  - Basic Pitch's model by Spotify, Apache-2.0, in the ONNX export Spotify ships
    with it (https://github.com/spotify/basic-pitch).
  - Audiobox Aesthetics by Meta, CC BY 4.0
    (https://huggingface.co/facebook/audiobox-aesthetics), part of its code from
    Microsoft's WavLM (MIT), in the ONNX export by Microck, CC BY 4.0
    (https://huggingface.co/Microck/audiobox-aesthetics-onnx), its MatMul
    weights quantized to int8.

The command palette's embedding model, fetched from the Hugging Face Hub the
first time the palette is typed in, checked against pinned SHA-256 hashes, and
kept as claudius's own smaller file of it (its numbers a byte each), which the
website also serves to its demo:

  - Model2Vec's potion-base-8M by Minish Lab, MIT
    (https://huggingface.co/minishlab/potion-base-8M), distilled from BAAI's
    bge-base-en-v1.5 (MIT) and trained with Tokenlearn. Its licence is in
    crates/claudius-intent/LICENSE-potion-base-8M, and the website serves it
    beside its copy.

The sample packs, fetched by `claudius setup` or `claudius-packs install`. Each
pack's licence and attribution are recorded in crates/claudius-packs/src/registry.json
and in the pack's index.json once installed; `claudius-packs list` prints them.
Songs that use packs whose licence asks for credit (CC BY) get a credits.txt
next to them. The default packs are by Alexander Holm (Salamander grand piano,
CC BY 3.0), Greg Sullivan (electric pianos, CC BY 3.0), Jeff Learman (jRhodes),
Versilian Studios (VSCO 2 and VCSL, CC0), Michael Fischer (TR-808, CC0),
Audio Realism (TR-909), Lars Muldjord (drum kit, CC BY 4.0), FreePats (CC0),
D. Smolken (double bass, CC0), Karoryfer (bass and voice, CC0), and the TR-707
and uzu kits (public domain, Unlicense). The piano SFZ mappings are by kinwie /
sfzinstruments.


Used where it is installed, never copied
----------------------------------------

Apple Loops, when GarageBand or Logic content is installed. Apple licenses them
for use in your own music. claudius reads them where they are installed and
keeps only one-shot cuts in its cache; it does not redistribute them.
